{
  "tabs": [
    {
      "id": "home",
      "title": "Home",
      "content": [
        {
          "id": "welcome",
          "title": "Welcome to ANQL",
          "description": "ANQL is a powerful visual document editor that allows you to create and organize your ideas intuitively.",
          "image": "docs/Help/Assets/homepage.png"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "create-node",
      "title": "Create Node",
      "content": [
        {
          "id": "autocomplete",
          "title": "Node creation on autocomplete",
          "description": [
            "Type the node name directly then press TAB to confirm.",
            "",
            "Available node types:",
            "- Code: Insert code blocks with syntax highlighting",
            "- Line: Add horizontal separators",
            "- Image: Insert images from URLs or files",
            "- Table: Create structured tables",
            "- Heading 1: Main section headings",
            "- Heading 2: Subsection headings", 
            "- Heading 3: Minor headings",
            "- Number List: Ordered numbered lists",
            "- Bullet List: Unordered bullet lists",
            "- Check List: Todo/task lists with checkboxes",
            "- Quote: Block quotes for citations",
            "- Math: Mathematical operation and conversion",
            "- Help: Access to this documentation"
          ],
          "image": "docs/Help/Assets/autocomplete creating.png"
        },
        {
          "id": "node-menu",
          "title": "Node Creation by using menu",
          "description": [
            "Create a new node to start building your document.",
            "",
            "Click on the creation button to access the menu.",
            "Choose from the available options."
          ],
          "image": [
            "docs/Help/Assets/create node button.png",
            "docs/Help/Assets/create node menu.png"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "node-options",
      "title": "Node Options",
      "content": [
        {
          "id": "node-menu-button",
          "title": "Node Menu",
          "description": [
            "Each node has its own options menu to modify its properties and content.",
            "",
            "Access the menu by clicking on the node handle or using keyboard shortcuts.",
            "The menu provides various actions for manipulating and transforming nodes."
          ],
          "image": [
            "docs/Help/Assets/node menu button.png",
            "docs/Help/Assets/node menu.png"]
        },
        {
          "id": "transform-menu",
          "title": "Transform Node Type",
          "description": [
            "You can transform nodes into other node types.",
            "",
            "Transformation Rules:",
            " Only certain node types can be transformed",
            " Transformable types: paragraph, heading, quote, code, list, listitem",
            " Non-transformable types: image, table, math, line",
            " All selected nodes must be transformable for the menu to appear",
            "",
            "Available transformations:",
            "- Normal: Convert to paragraph (Ctrl+Alt+0 / Mac: ⌘⌥0)",
            "- Heading 1: Convert to main heading (Ctrl+Alt+1 / Mac: ⌘⌥1)",
            "- Heading 2: Convert to sub heading (Ctrl+Alt+2 / Mac: ⌘⌥2)",
            "- Heading 3: Convert to minor heading (Ctrl+Alt+3 / Mac: ⌘⌥3)",
            "- Number List: Convert to numbered list (Ctrl+Shift+7 / Mac: ⌘⇧7)",
            "- Bullet List: Convert to bullet list (Ctrl+Shift+8 / Mac: ⌘⇧8)",
            "- Check List: Convert to todo list (Ctrl+Shift+9 / Mac: ⌘⇧9)",
            "- Quote: Convert to block quote (Ctrl+Shift+. / Mac: ⌘⇧.)",
            "- Code: Convert to code block (Ctrl+Alt+C / Mac: ⌘⌥C)"
          ],
          "image": "docs/Help/Assets/transform.png"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "math-expressions",
      "title": "Mathematical Expressions",
      "content": [
        {
          "id": "math-intro",
          "title": "Introduction to Math Nodes",
          "description": [
            "Math nodes allow you to perform mathematical calculations and define variables within your document.",
            "",
            "The math functionality is powered by mathjs, a powerful mathematics library that supports a wide range of operations.",
            "",
            "Results are calculated in real-time as you type and displayed below the expression."
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "basic-operations",
          "title": "Basic Arithmetic Operations",
          "description": [
            "You can perform standard arithmetic operations:",
            "",
            "- Addition: 2 + 3",
            "- Subtraction: 10 - 4",
            "- Multiplication: 6 * 7",
            "- Division: 15 / 3",
            "- Power: 2 ^ 3",
            "- Modulo: 17 % 5",
            "",
            "Complex expressions are also supported:",
            "- (5 + 3) * 2",
            "- 10 / (2 + 3)",
            "- 2 ^ (3 + 1)"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "variables",
          "title": "Variable Assignment and Usage",
          "description": [
            "Define variables using the assignment syntax and use them in subsequent expressions:",
            "",
            "Syntax: variable_name = expression",
            "",
            "Examples:",
            "- x = 10",
            "- y = 5",
            "- z = x + y  (result: 15)",
            "- area = x * y  (result: 50)",
            "",
            "Variable naming rules:",
            "- Must start with a letter or underscore",
            "- Can contain letters, numbers, and underscores",
            "- Case-sensitive (x and X are different variables)"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "advanced-functions",
          "title": "Advanced Mathematical Functions",
          "description": [
            "Mathjs provides many built-in functions:",
            "",
            "Trigonometric functions:",
            "- sin(0.5)",
            "- cos(1)",
            "- tan(0.25)",
            "",
            "Other functions:",
            "- sqrt(16)  (square root)",
            "- abs(-5)  (absolute value)",
            "- log(100)  (logarithm)",
            "- exp(2)  (exponential)",
            "- floor(3.7)  (round down)",
            "- ceil(3.2)  (round up)",
            "- round(3.5)  (round to nearest)"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "constants",
          "title": "Mathematical Constants",
          "description": [
            "Use built-in mathematical constants:",
            "",
            "- pi  (π ≈ 3.14159)",
            "- e  (Euler's number ≈ 2.71828)",
            "",
            "Examples:",
            "- 2 * pi",
            "- e ^ 2",
            "- sin(pi/2)"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "symbolic-computation",
          "title": "Symbolic Computation (Advanced)",
          "description": [
            "Mathjs supports symbolic computation for algebraic operations:",
            "",
            "Simplify expressions:",
            "- simplify('3 + 2 / 4')  → '7 / 2'",
            "- simplify('2x + 3x')  → '5 * x'",
            "- simplify('x^2 + x + 3 + x^2')  → '2 * x ^ 2 + x + 3'",
            "",
            "Calculate derivatives:",
            "- derivative('x^2', 'x')  → '2 * x'",
            "- derivative('sin(2x)', 'x')  → '2 * cos(2 * x)'",
            "- derivative('2x^2 + 3x + 4', 'x')  → '4 * x + 3'",
            "",
            "Note: These advanced symbolic functions are available in mathjs but may require specific implementation in your current setup."
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "matrix-operations",
          "title": "Matrix and Vector Operations",
          "description": [
            "Mathjs supports matrix and vector operations:",
            "",
            "Matrix creation:",
            "- matrix([1, 2, 3])",
            "- matrix([[1, 2], [3, 4]])",
            "",
            "Matrix operations:",
            "- matrix addition: A + B",
            "- matrix multiplication: A * B",
            "- matrix transpose: transpose(A)",
            "- matrix determinant: det(A)",
            "- matrix inverse: inv(A)",
            "",
            "Vector operations:",
            "- dot product: dot(a, b)",
            "- cross product: cross(a, b)",
            "- norm: norm(v)"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "additional-functions",
          "title": "Additional Mathematical Functions",
          "description": [
            "Mathjs provides many more functions:",
            "",
            "Statistics:",
            "- mean([1, 2, 3, 4, 5])",
            "- median([1, 2, 3, 4, 5])",
            "- std([1, 2, 3, 4, 5])",
            "- variance([1, 2, 3, 4, 5])",
            "",
            "Complex numbers:",
            "- complex(2, 3)",
            "- re(complex(2, 3))",
            "- im(complex(2, 3))",
            "",
            "Units:",
            "- unit('5 cm')",
            "- unit('2 kg').to('g')",
            "- unit('10 m/s') * unit('5 s')"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "error-handling",
          "title": "Error Handling",
          "description": [
            "Math nodes provide visual feedback for errors:",
            "",
            "Common errors:",
            "- Division by zero: 5 / 0",
            "- Invalid syntax: 2 + * 3",
            "- Undefined variables: unknown_var + 5",
            "- Invalid values: sqrt(-1)",
            "",
            "Error display:",
            "- Errors appear in red at the bottom of the math node",
            "- Click on the error message to see full details",
            "- Results are automatically hidden when errors occur"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "math-examples",
          "title": "Practical Examples",
          "description": [
            "Example 1: Simple calculations",
            "price = 100",
            "tax = 0.2",
            "total = price * (1 + tax)  (result: 120)",
            "",
            "Example 2: Geometry calculations",
            "radius = 5",
            "area = pi * radius ^ 2  (result: 78.5398)",
            "circumference = 2 * pi * radius  (result: 31.4159)",
            "",
            "Example 3: Financial calculations",
            "principal = 1000",
            "rate = 0.05",
            "years = 3",
            "amount = principal * (1 + rate) ^ years  (result: 1157.625)"
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
